From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: Keep the largest size when merging ranges

generateConfiguration() sorts each format's size ranges by their minimum
and merges overlapping neighbours, assuming a range that starts later
also ends later. With the software ISP every range starts at the Bayer
pattern size, so all of them overlap, the sort leaves them in any order,
and the merged range ends at whichever came last, not at the largest.

On a Zinwa Q25 the IMX111's processed formats then ended at 1276x720,
from its 1280x720 mode, instead of 3276x2464, so no 4:3 size above
800x600 was offered.

Merge to the larger of both maximums.
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index 6b4e1dbc..8b1b43be 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1537,7 +1537,7 @@ SimplePipelineHandler::generateConfiguration(Camera *camera, std::span<const Str
 			while (++next != sizes.end()) {
 				if (cur->max.width >= next->min.width &&
 				    cur->max.height >= next->min.height)
-					cur->max = next->max;
+					cur->max = cur->max.expandedTo(next->max);
 				else if (++cur != next)
 					*cur = *next;
 			}
